    <div id="m5-view-design-challenge" class="agentic-design-subview" style="display: none;">
        <div class="card glass-panel" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                <span style="font-size: 1.6rem;">❓</span>
                <div>
                    <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.35rem; color: #f8fafc;">
                        Production Challenge Diagnostic: Which Layer Breaks in Production?
                    </h3>
                    <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.88rem;">
                        "Which layer do you think is the most challenging to implement in production — Memory, Orchestration, Governance, or Reliability?"
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.25rem;">
                <!-- Challenger 1: Memory -->
                <div style="background: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                        <span style="font-size: 1.3rem;">🧠</span>
                        <strong style="color: #c4b5fd; font-size: 1.05rem;">Memory Challenges</strong>
                    </div>
                    <ul style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.83rem; line-height: 1.5; padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 0.85rem 0;">
                        <li><strong>Semantic Drift:</strong> Old memories contradict new user inputs.</li>
                        <li><strong>Context Dilution:</strong> Unpruned recall fills the attention window, degrading reasoning.</li>
                        <li><strong>Multi-Tenant Leakage:</strong> Shared vector namespaces leaking cross-customer PII.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #34d399; font-weight: 600;">
                        ✓ Fix: Strict namespace ACLs, decaying recency weights, Mem0 episodic summarization.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Challenger 2: Orchestration -->
                <div style="background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                        <span style="font-size: 1.3rem;">🎯</span>
                        <strong style="color: #38bdf8; font-size: 1.05rem;">Orchestration Challenges</strong>
                    </div>
                    <ul style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.83rem; line-height: 1.5; padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 0.85rem 0;">
                        <li><strong>Infinite Loops:</strong> Agent cycles between identical failing tool arguments.</li>
                        <li><strong>Multi-Agent Deadlock:</strong> Agent A waits for Agent B while Agent B awaits Agent A.</li>
                        <li><strong>Non-Deterministic Flapping:</strong> Same goal yields completely divergent task sequences.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #34d399; font-weight: 600;">
                        ✓ Fix: Hard cycle limits (\\(N \\le 6\\)), state checkpointer rollbacks, Pregel deterministic DAGs.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Challenger 3: Reliability -->
                <div style="background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                        <span style="font-size: 1.3rem;">🔄</span>
                        <strong style="color: #f87171; font-size: 1.05rem;">Reliability Challenges</strong>
                    </div>
                    <ul style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.83rem; line-height: 1.5; padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 0.85rem 0;">
                        <li><strong>External API Flakiness:</strong> SaaS rate limits, 503 gateway timeouts, network blips.</li>
                        <li><strong>Malformed Arguments:</strong> LLM hallucinating invalid JSON keys into tool callers.</li>
                        <li><strong>Silent Cascades:</strong> Upstream bad tool output contaminating all subsequent agent steps.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #34d399; font-weight: 600;">
                        ✓ Fix: Exponential backoff + jitter, Pydantic tool validation, Human-in-the-Loop circuit breakers.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Challenger 4: Governance -->
                <div style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                        <span style="font-size: 1.3rem;">⚖️</span>
                        <strong style="color: #fbbf24; font-size: 1.05rem;">Governance Challenges</strong>
                    </div>
                    <ul style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.83rem; line-height: 1.5; padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 0.85rem 0;">
                        <li><strong>Prompt Injection Privilege Escalation:</strong> Untrusted web content instructing agent to DROP database.</li>
                        <li><strong>Unbounded Financial Spend:</strong> Agent calling expensive endpoints 500 times in batch.</li>
                        <li><strong>Compliance Gaps:</strong> Inability to provide auditor with reproducible decision traces.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #34d399; font-weight: 600;">
                        ✓ Fix: Declarative Open Policy Agent (OPA) gates, read-only database roles, immutable WORM logs.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

